# VPN_SWITCH_USER_openvpn - Privilege-drop user for OpenVPN configs
#
# Optional user name enforced in patched OpenVPN configs via the
# "user" directive. Follows the VPN_SWITCH_USER_<protocol> naming
# convention (WireGuard has no equivalent: it runs in the kernel and
# has no userspace daemon that could drop privileges).
#
# Default: (empty - "user" directives in configs are left unchanged)
#
# If set, vpn-switch patches configs at connect time:
#   - Existing "user" directives are rewritten to this value
#   - If no "user" directive exists, one is appended
#
# Example:
#   openvpn
#
# Background:
#   The FreeBSD openvpn port >= 2.7 ships a dedicated "openvpn"
#   user/group and recommends migrating configs away from "nobody".
#
# Caveat:
#   Dropping privileges requires "persist-key" and "persist-tun" in
#   the config for restarts/renegotiation to work. Most provider
#   configs include these; verify before enabling.
